+Bottom nav root cause: the pill was centred with the individual
+'translate: -50% 0' property while the same rule used 'transform'
+for the auto-hide animation. The Tailwind/LightningCSS pipeline
+merges the two when compiling, and the merged output drops the
+-50% shift — leaving 'left: 50%' with no compensating translate,
+so the pill anchored at mid-viewport and its right half (and the
+icons in it) fell off-screen.
+
+Fix, decoupling the two jobs for good:
+
+- New outer .dock-wrap: position fixed, left 0 / right 0,
+  bottom max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-bottom) + 12px),
+  display flex, justify-content center, pointer-events none.
+  It only centres.
+- The nav pill inside keeps pointer-events auto and now only
+  ever transforms on the Y axis for hide/show, so the animation
+  can never touch its horizontal position. No translate
+  property, no left:50%, no fixed px widths remain.
