+## What the fix does (for the PR description)
+
+**Root cause of the off-center dock:** the pill was centred with the
+individual `translate: -50% 0` property while the *same* CSS rule used
+`transform` for the auto-hide animation. The Tailwind v4 / LightningCSS
+pipeline merges the two at compile time and the merged output drops the
+-50% shift, leaving `left: 50%` with no compensating translate — the pill
+anchored at mid-viewport and its right half (3 icons) fell off-screen.
+
+**Fix:**
+
+- Outer `.dock-wrap`: `position: fixed; left: 0; right: 0;
+  bottom: max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-bottom) + 12px); display: flex;
+  justify-content: center; pointer-events: none`. It only centres.
+- Inner `nav.dock` pill: `pointer-events: auto; width: min(100% - 24px, 420px)`
+  (480px cap on tablets, 400px in short landscape); the hide/show transform is
+  now Y-only, so it can never affect horizontal position. All 6 items are
+  `flex: 1; min-width: 0` with ≥44px touch targets at 320/360/390/430/768px.
+- Mobile header: identical look, now `position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0;
+  right: 0` with `padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top)`; never hides on
+  scroll; z-index above the feed, below modals/viewers. Page content gets
+  `padding-top: calc(60px + env(safe-area-inset-top))`.
+- Heights use `dvh`. Glass styling, auto-hide on scroll down / show on scroll
+  up, routes, features, backend and the desktop layout are unchanged.
